[Event "Caro-Kann Classical"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Classical Variation"]
[ECO "B18"]
[Origin "Horatio Caro & Marcus Kann (1886)"]
[Side "black"]
[Tags "e4,caro-kann,solid"]
[Difficulty "2"]

1. e4 c6 { The Caro-Kann: ...c6 prepares ...d5 while keeping the light-squared bishop free. }
2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 { [%name Classical, 4...Bf5] The bishop develops actively before ...e6 locks it in. }
( 4... Nd7 { [%name Karpov, 4...Nd7] Preparing ...Ngf6 so that a trade on f6 does not damage Black's pawns. }
  5. Ng5 Ngf6 6. Bd3 e6 7. N1f3 Bd6 8. Qe2 h6 9. Ne4 Nxe4 10. Qxe4 { Black is solid and will free the game with ...c5 or ...e5. } )
5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 h6 { Without ...h6, h5 would trap the bishop. }
7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 { Black has traded the problem bishop and has a very solid position. }
11. Bd2 Ngf6 12. O-O-O Be7 { Black castles short and plays for ...c5 or ...Qc7 and ...O-O-O. } *
